WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.510
What is the cloud?

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:05.860
It's data.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.580
It's scalable.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.560
It's elastic.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:13.240
It's servers, databases, and hard drives.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:17.680
But it's bound in physical data centers.
We're going to unveil something that

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.500
completely changes the way you think about cloud.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.960
You know public cloud and you may know
private cloud. And you might even know

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:28.960
about hybrid clouds, and marketing
clouds, and elastic clouds

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.970
,but today, now,

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.140
there's Actual Cloud.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.390
Introducing

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.950
Google Actual Cloud Platform. 

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.920
This is the world’s first cloud offering                     running on servers in the troposphere,

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:45.680
inside actual clouds. 

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.940
It's faster, it's more scalable, it's more secure,                                                    and most importantly

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.960
it looks like a real cloud.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.540
We're also releasing an industry first
performance feature

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:58.520
Stormboost. 

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.160
Stormboost draws on the
power of Mother Nature

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:05.430
to give your persistent disks a 50%
IOPS boost during thunderstorms.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:09.110
And you can predict storage performance
right from the Developers Console

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.670
by monitoring our new weather dashboard.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.730
Or, you can just look out the window.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:19.800
Google Actual Cloud Platform is the
culmination of groundbreaking scientific research

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.580
on supercooled water droplets,
technological breakthroughs in

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.860
high-altitude

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:28.710
ultra-low pressure chip design, and
operational efficiencies

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:32.290
related to the way we run
non-terrestrial datacenters.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:37.640
I sleep more soundly knowing that my data is
30,000 feet above the ground.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.479
I just love that I can see it.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:46.740
This is the first step in an exciting
journey. People say the sky's the limit

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.580
but we think bigger.

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:53.830
The clouds are so pretty.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.610
That's not just a cloud, Honey.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.430
That's Google Actual Cloud Platform.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:00.950
okay

